WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.360
Good morning Hank it's Tuesday. It's Question Tuesday, the day that I answer real questions from real nerd fighters.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:05.600
So let's get right to it. "What're you reading?"

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.220
Well I just read an amazing book by a first novelist named Hank Green.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.500
I don't want to say anything more until it's available for preorder

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.740
but wow it's like...properly brilliant.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.780
And now I'm reading An Introduction to Global Health Delivery,

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.500
which is quite different from Hank's book, but also excellent.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.040
"What's your favorite song at the moment?"

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:26.080
So my kids have discovered that their uncle Hank is a musician whose songs you can listen to on Spotify

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.100
and they won't stop listening to him.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.540
I've probably heard "This isn't Hogwarts" 10,000 times in the last two weeks.

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:33.760
And I have to say, it's pretty darn good.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.680
Is this becoming a Hank Green appreciation vlog?! No more Hank for the rest of the video.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.620
"Thoughts on Brexit and pears?" Now that is a Question Tuesday question.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.020
So sometimes I'll be at the grocery store and I'll think "you know what future me would like to eat?"

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.280
Pears. A ton of pears.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.560
So I'll buy a bunch of pears.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.540
And then later when I am future me I'll open up the refrigerator and I'll think:

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:57.260
"Ugh I really wish I hadn't gotten these pears, I wish I could just return them and get my money back.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.220
"Because I completely misapprehended my appetite for pears!"

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:01.920
But you can't return pears.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.920
Speaking of which, "pears or apples?"

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.460
Hmm I don't know if we're still talking about Brexit but regardless, apples.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:12.740
"In Turtles All the Way Down, how can Daisy say that Attack of the Clones is the most underrated Star Wars Movie?"

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:13.640
That's the stupidest thing I've ever heard.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.120
I'm going to try not to respond to hostility with hostility here

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:20.260
but look, Daisy's wrong about a lot of things but she's right about this.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:23.940
Empire Strikes Back: correctly rated as the best Star Wars movie.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.960
A New Hope, also correctly rated as excellent.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.180
Return of the Jedi is if anything slightly overrated.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:31.120
Rogue One and The Force Awakens are both rated correctly.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:34.220
The Phantom Menace is correctly rated as THE WORST.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:38.120
Revenge of the Sith widely and appropriately believed to be the best of the prequels.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:44.040
Leaving Attack of the Clones as the only and ergo the most underrated Star Wars movie.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.560
"Hey John, you working on anything new?"

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:48.800
Yeah I've got a new series over at Hank Games called John Green solves your problems

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.280
in which I play FIFA while solving people's problems.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:54.900
So far I've solved the problem of somebody who couldn't reach the spot on their back that itched.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.520
And someone else whose taste was too expensive for their budget.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:01.600
But over the course of many episodes I'm hoping, you know, to solve all of the problems.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:03.880
"Hey, which charities one the Project for Awesome money?

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:08.560
These 25 charities will all be getting grants from this year's Project for Awesome.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.300
Congratulations to them and thank you again to everyone who donated.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.740
"How do you deal with stress?"

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:13.240
Poorly.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:14.580
"Favorite Winona Ryder movie?"

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:15.260
Heathers.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:16.100
"Are you having a midlife crisis yet?"

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.540
Maybe a little bit.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:19.760
"How important is nature to you?"

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:23.840
I think the thing to remember is that we are nature just as much as, like, birds and trees are.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:25.760
So...very important.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.260
"Why isn't there any Turtles All the Way Down merch?"

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:33.400
There is, at DFTBA.com! You can find amazing posters and also a wonderful pencil set with quotes from the book.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.680
"Favorite Marvel character?" Probably the Hulk.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.140
"Favorite DC character?"

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:38.160
Right now, probably Paul Manafort.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.340
I cannot look away from the Paul Manafort storyline.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.600
"Are you upset about this?"

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.480
No I'm just glad my books can be useful.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.620
"When did you get a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame?"

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:53.700
I didn't, that star belongs to the John Green who won 5 Oscars, not me who once won an MTV movie award.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.860
"What is the most likely way for humans to go extinct?"

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.820
This is a question I spend a fair amount of time thinking about.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:04.620
I think disease is most likely followed by some kind of AI or post-human species rendering us obsolete.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.260
Followed by an extinction-level war.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:09.920
Basically, I think it's still it's most likely that microorganisms will be our undoing.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:14.460
But I think there's a growing possibility that we will be our own undoing.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.220
"How do you stop worrying about not living your life to the fullest?"

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:21.600
Well I don't know how to stop worrying but I do think the idea of living your life to the fullest is a little flawed.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:25.160
Like, why is jumping out of an airplane inherently better than reading a book?

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:30.440
Or why is living a life that looks good on Instagram inherently more meaningful than a life lived quietly?

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.660
I just don't buy it. Like Eurdora Welty wrote:

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:38.100
"A sheltered life can be a daring life as well, for all serious daring starts from within."

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.160
So live your life.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:40.912
Hank, I will see you on Friday.

